   "body": "**Operator feedback (2026-11-18), added to this issue (same screen):** the « Thème » choice (Clair / Sombre / Système) becomes **three image tiles** side by side instead of a menu.\n\n- Each tile is a small mock screen: a rounded card with two text lines and a coloured dot, and the label below it (« Clair », « Sombre », « Système »). The selected tile has an accent-coloured outline and label.\n- **Clair** draws the current light style (Blanc or Doux). **Sombre** draws the current dark style (Standard grey, Plus sombre or OLED, with the brightness). **Système** is split diagonally between the two.\n- **The dot is the chosen accent colour**, updated live with the hue slider.\n- Built with SwiftUI shapes from the theme tokens (no bitmap assets). It is a single-choice control for VoiceOver: each tile is a button with the selected trait, labelled « Thème clair », « Thème sombre » or « Thème du système ». At Dynamic Type XL the tiles wrap or scale without clipping.\n- Test: the tile colours come from the same surfaces as the reader preview, the dot from the accent, and selection sets the setting.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
