   "body": "·/·r·elease cloud/i1038-sonnet\n\nHand-off (operator asked to write everything down; the orchestrator lost the link). **Where it stands: PR #1219, draft, Compile check green, review round 2 not run.**\n\n- **PR:** #1219, head `a2a9ca259fe339e3751300912a1b5fb16ce8a4ff`, draft, `compile-check` label on, **stacked on #1212** (base `fix/1210-dark-grey`, same files: `ThemeAppearance`, `reader.css`). Compile check **green** on that head (run 44471370763); « App build + tests » and « HFRKit tests (macOS) » are red only because the PR is a draft (the gate fails on purpose). `swiftlint --strict` clean; `swift test` on the touched HFRKit suites passed (35 tests, Linux). **No app test has ever run** (Linux, no Xcode).\n- **Opus 5.5 review:** round 1 REQUEST CHANGES on `f46de0dd` (missing `import HFRStorage`, the script test, softLight dark side, docs, a dead variable, tile-selection test), all fixed in `b9aca2dd`; then one compile fix (`a2a9ca25`: a literal comment in `#expect`). **Round 2 has not been run**; there are 2 rounds left (cap 3).\n- **What it does:** `LightStyle` (Blanc default, Doux), device setting `theme_light_style` with tolerant decoding; Doux's warm surfaces (page `#F5F4EF`, placeholder `#E9E7DE`, separator `#D6D3C8`, secondary `#636366`, proposed values for the operator to validate on a screenshot) in the reader, the web view layer and the native screen fill (`ScreenFill.softLight`); the Réglages › Thème controls follow « Thème » (Clair: light style + preview; Sombre: dark style + brightness; Système: both, titled); « Thème » as three SwiftUI tiles (Clair, Sombre, Système split diagonally), VoiceOver single-choice, wrapping at large Dynamic Type; ADR 0013 matrix, `THEMES.md`, a `gap-new` row GAP-1213.\n- **What is left:**\n  1. After #1212 merges: retarget #1219 to `dev-swift`, merge `dev-swift` into the branch (`git show --remerge-diff` must be empty to keep an APPROVE).\n  2. Opus review round 2 (model explicit, `adversarial-reviewer`), fix, then the ready line on #893.\n  3. Screenshots (Réglages › Thème in the three modes, the reader in Doux) and the device check on #893; the operator validates Doux's values.\n  4. Merge, then close with `Done in #1219 (merged as <sha>)`.\n- **Not covered, stated in the PR and as follow-ups:** the default cyan day accent is 1.52:1 on white and 1.38:1 on Doux (#1220); native list rows stay white on the Doux page (#1221); « quotes a step darker » is not drawn (the default quote has no fill, #819).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
